  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (RNA-only, multiprofile, PCA n2000, avgpool) is the best result so far at 0.591 acc, showing multiprofile+avgpool is the strongest RNA configuration. Image-only (config_010) is very weak (0.208), suggesting the image modality may contribute little signal. Uncertainty: We have only tested PCA n2000 as the RNA encoder; it is unclear whether a learned nonlinear encoder (scvi_n200) captures complementary biological signal that PCA misses. This experiment (config_005: scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) is a clean controlled comparison to config_002, changing only the RNA encoder. It will clarify whether encoder choice is a meaningful design axis before we invest limited budget in multimodal fusion experiments. If scvi substantially outperforms PCA, we know to prioritize it in multimodal configs; if it does not, PCA is sufficient and we can focus remaining budget on testing whether multimodal fusion adds value at all."
}

